#: src/macros/proc-macros/welcome.md:6
msgid "Procedural Macros"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/welcome.md:8
msgid ""
"**Procedural macros** are far more powerful than declarative macros. Instead "
"of matching syntax templates, they are literal compiler plugins:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/welcome.md:11
msgid ""
"They are implemented as functions that receive one or two **token streams** "
"and return a **token stream**."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/welcome.md:13
msgid "They are written in standard, fully featured Rust."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/welcome.md:14
msgid ""
"They have complete programmatic access to the incoming token stream, "
"allowing you to parse, modify, or generate complex code structures."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/welcome.md:16
msgid ""
"They require a dedicated library crate configured with `proc-macro = true` "
"in its `Cargo.toml`."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/welcome.md:19
msgid ""
"We will explore how procedural macros are defined, how they compile, and how "
"to write them."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/welcome.md:25
msgid ""
"Explain that procedural macros are called \"procedural\" because they "
"execute standard Rust procedures (functions) to transform code at compile "
"time."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/welcome.md:27
msgid ""
"Emphasize that because they are compiled as libraries and loaded by the "
"compiler during build time, they have a heavier impact on compilation speed "
"compared to declarative macros."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/welcome.md:30
msgid ""
"This slide serves as a transition into the detailed mechanics of procedural "
"macros."
msgstr ""
